# Default dashboard column autosizing
Workstream-ID: lea-24
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/24
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed bounded dashboard table-layout improvement
Status: DONE
Milestone: Size dashboard columns to their content on first display
Dependencies: lea-09

## Purpose
Use native content-based column sizing throughout the dashboard, including
read-only tables and the resume-correction and outreach editors. Remove fixed
review-column widths without changing data, approvals or outreach behavior.

## Tasks
- [x] Inventory dashboard table renderers and verify the installed sizing API.
- [x] Apply content-sized layouts consistently and remove fixed column widths.
- [x] Cover initial sizing and retained editing behavior with fictional fixtures.
- [x] Check real-browser sizing, reruns and narrow-view horizontal scrolling.
- [x] Update directly affected guides and reconcile scoped tracking.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Every dashboard table starts with native content-based column widths.
- [x] Resume review no longer fixes Question or Why to preset widths.
- [x] Checkbox types, links, disabled columns, row identity and save actions remain intact.
- [x] Wide tables stay usable with horizontal scrolling and manual resizing.
- [x] Qualification uses fictional data without driving independent user applications.
- [x] Existing report controls, private inputs, older workstreams and releases are preserved.
- [x] One repository issue, one correctly staged Project item and a durable backlink represent the workstream.

## Completion evidence
All twelve read-only dataframe and two editable table renderers now use native
content-width layouts. The two fixed resume-review column presets are removed;
types, disabled columns, keys, row identity and persistence actions are unchanged.

Black, Ruff and mypy pass. All 35 affected cases pass, including four focused
table cases and the existing Reports/focus regressions. Three sizing regressions
reproduce the old stretch/preset behavior.

A fresh headless browser verifies all fourteen actual table layouts, fourteen
native sizing interactions, ordinary header resizing, reload defaults and
horizontal scrolling at a narrow viewport without page overflow. Ordinary
text editing, approval and save persist a fictional correction; an ordinary
outreach checkbox/completion action removes only the fictional draft. Rendering
and sizing alone leave database bytes unchanged. Both layout screenshots were
reviewed.

Native automatic sizing has a limit: in the tested Streamlit 1.60 grid, a long
column initially measures 500 pixels while manual Autosize measures 565.
Default content sizing is not a promise to expose arbitrarily long text.
Eight directly affected guides explain native sizing, scrolling and adjustments.

The existing local Reports repair, older workstream records, private setup and
published release remain preserved. Declare bounded technical completion for
scoped tracking reconciliation; retain final settlement separately from this
managed description. No commit, push, new release, live-site qualification or
human acceptance is claimed.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-10: Started the bounded default-autosizing improvement. Preserve the
  completed local Reports repair, private setup and independently running
  applications. Use a disposable loopback fixture and fresh browser context.
- 2026-11-10: Completed native sizing, focused source gates, actual fictional
  browser edit/save qualification and eight affected guides. Browser checks
  respect the native automatic-width cap and await actual backend reruns;
  frontend-only checkbox state is not evidence that a save has completed.
